# Setup nstack

Review and change the model{% if harness != "claude" %} and effort{% endif %} nstack uses for each delegated role in this client, then check the client runs them. Every role has a built-in default, so this is optional.

nstack's plugin hook reads the `[nstack role=<role> seat=<n>]` tag on each launch of `nstack-agent`, sets the role's model{% if harness != "claude" %} and effort{% endif %}, and routes read-only roles to `nstack-reader`. At session start it adds an `nstack panels` line with each panel's seats. Overrides live in `~/.nstack/models.json`, per client. Model changes apply to the next launch, seat counts to new sessions.

Never hand-write `models.json`. Use the hook's script, `<helper>`: {% if harness == "claude" %}`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/nstack_config.py`{% elif harness == "codex" %}`../../hooks/nstack_config.py` from this skill's base directory (absolute path){% else %}`../../com.github.copilot/hooks/nstack_config.py` from this skill's base directory (absolute path){% endif %}. It needs Python 3.11 or newer.

Open a todolist with one entry per step before starting.

## 1. Load the current state

Run `python3 --version`, then `python3 <helper> roles` (catalog, defaults, effort levels) and `python3 <helper> status` (effective model, effort, source, and verification per seat). Stop on Python below 3.11, or on `"ok": false` and show its `message` and `repair`.
{% if harness == "codex" %}
Codex runs plugin hooks only once trusted. If nstack's hook is untrusted, have the user trust it in `/hooks` first. Until then nstack agents reply that the hook did not run.
{% endif %}
## 2. Choose overrides

Show a table of every role with its model, effort, and source. Ask which to change with {{ ask_user }}.

{% if harness == "claude" -%}
Claude Code takes only `sonnet`, `opus`, `haiku`, `fable`, or `inherit` (the main model) per launch, and no per-launch effort.
{%- elif harness == "codex" -%}
Use model ids from the Codex model picker, or `inherit`. Effort is `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`, or `ultra`, where the model supports it.
{%- else -%}
Use model ids as Copilot lists them (`claude-opus-5.5`, `gpt-6.1-sol`), or `inherit`. They work in Copilot CLI and VS Code Agent Host alike. Effort is `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, or `max`, where the model supports it.
{%- endif %} Never set a model the user hasn't confirmed they can use.

Panel roles take 2 to 6 seats (`candidate-graft-judge` 1 to 6). Repeating a model across seats gives independent attempts, not model diversity. Say so.

## 3. Preview

Write the overrides to a temp JSON file outside the repository. It replaces this client's overrides as a whole, so list every role that should differ from its default. Empty `roles` clears them.

```json
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "clients": {
    "{{ harness }}": {
      "roles": {
        "review-panel-reviewer": [{"model": "<model-a>"{% if harness != "claude" %}, "effort": "high"{% endif %}}, {"model": "<model-b>"{% if harness != "claude" %}, "effort": "high"{% endif %}}]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Run `python3 <helper> configure --input <overrides.json> --dry-run` and show each changed role's `before` and `after`. Fix validation errors with the user and preview again.

## 4. Apply

After the user confirms, run `python3 <helper> configure --input <overrides.json> --apply --plan-id <plan_id>`. On `stale_plan` (exit 5), preview again and get fresh confirmation. Delete the temp file.

## 5. Check dispatch

A configured model is not proof the client runs it. Probe at least one seat per distinct model with {{ launch('nstack:implementation:nstack-agent', '[nstack role=<role> seat=<n>]') }} and this brief:

```text
[nstack role=<role> seat=<n>] This is an nstack setup probe. Do not read, write, or run anything.
Reply with exactly one line: NSTACK-PROBE <role> <seat>
```

Record the result with `python3 <helper> record-verification --role <role> --seat <n> --status <verified|failed> --evidence "<observation>"`. Record `failed` when the launch is blocked or the model is rejected, and show the error. Record `verified` only when the client shows which model served the launch{% if harness == "claude" %} (`resolvedModel` in the launch result, or the usage report){% elif harness == "codex" %} (the subagent's thread details){% else %} (the subagent's model in the session log or timeline){% endif %}, and quote it. A subagent's claim about its own model is not evidence. Otherwise leave the seat unverified.

## 6. Report

The overrides applied (or defaults in use), the effective model and effort per role from `status`, each probed seat as verified, failed, or unverified with the reason, and anything still blocked{% if harness == "codex" %}, including an untrusted hook{% endif %}. Re-running is safe; unchanged choices write nothing.
